.TH BNLEARN 1 2000-1月 "knockouts" "knockouts"
.SH NAME
knockouts \- run the in silico gene knockout experiment on the given network model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIknockouts(\fBbnlearn\fR as <generic> InsilicoPerturbationExperiment, 
\fBgeneNames\fR as any);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
run the in silico gene knockout experiment on the given network model
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBbnlearn\fB \fR\- 
 the trained network model object, which could be created by the \fBbnlearn\fR 
 api or the \fBGEARS::new\fR api.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneNames\fB \fR\- 
 a character vector of the gene id for run the knockout experiment, one 
 @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.Intervention.InterventionResult\fR object will be generated for each gene.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a vector of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.Intervention.InterventionResult\fR perturbation result: the 
 \fBWildtypeMeans\fR is the wildtype expression value of each gene, the 
 \fBMutantMeans\fR is the expression value of each gene after the gene has been 
 knocked out, and the \fBFoldChanges\fR, \fBPercentChanges\fR, \fBZScores\fR and 
 \fBIsSignificant\fR data is the differential analysis result of the 
 perturbation.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the behavior of this function is determined by the \fBstrict\fR option of the 
 input network model: an error will be thrown when the target gene is missing 
 from the network model in the strict mode, otherwise the wildtype expression 
 data will be returned as the result with the \fBUndefined\fR flag marked as 
 TRUE.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bnlearn
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
